  <description>&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;Official corporate product brochure and comprehensive technical specification comparison matrix for the Aastra (now Mitel) 6700i and 9000 series enterprise-grade SIP desktop telephones. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;Hardware Profiles &amp;amp; Models Documented:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Aastra 6730i &amp;amp; 6731i: Entry-level, slimline 3-line LCD enterprise desk phones.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Aastra 6735i &amp;amp; 6737i: Gigabit Ethernet enabled variants featuring graphical displays and HD Audio capabilities.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Aastra 6739i: Premium flagship multimedia endpoint featuring a 5.7” Full VGA color touch screen, integrated Bluetooth, and USB connectivity.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Aastra 6753i, 6755i, &amp;amp; 6757i: Scalable high-density programmable display endpoints supporting M670i and M675i attendant expansion modules.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Aastra 9143i &amp;amp; 9480i: Legacy carrier-grade enterprise desktop variants.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;Technical Data and Feature Matrices Included:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Telephony Capacity: Configuration parameters detailing up to 9 lines with call appearance, multi-proxy registration tracks, and Busy Lamp Field (BLF) status handling.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Interface &amp;amp; Network Specs: Data covering integrated multi-port Gigabit Ethernet switching, 802.1p/q VLAN tagging, QoS marking, LLDP-MED, 802.1X network security, and configuration encryption parameters (3DES/tuz files).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Audio Engineering: Architectural comparison parameters separating Aastra Hi-Q™ wideband technology from high-definition (HD) audio hardware configurations across G.711, G.729, and G.722 codecs.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;- Provisioning Engine Specs: Validation guidelines highlighting central automated deployment structures across TFTP, FTP, and HTTP server paths.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);"&gt;Preserved for historical telecommunication hardware research, open-source PBX deployment references, enterprise IT firmware compatibility audits, and digital telephony documentation archiving.&lt;/div&gt;</description>
